    "body": "Both are correct :).\r\n\r\nThe current construction is an example of [English passive voice](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_passive_voice), in particular it looks like it's the \"Double passives\" construct. It's describing an action that should be done (\"to be included\"). The non-passive voice version would be \"Such specifications may require that rel's supported tokens include their link types\". But we use the passive voice version since it shifts the focus to the link types, instead of the supported tokens.\r\n\r\nThe \"are\" version would be a different construct, describing a state of the world that we want to be true. It's putting the focus not on the action (verb) of \"include\" (conjugated as \"(to) be included\"), but on the adjective \"included\".\r\n\r\nHope this helps?? Sorry about how terrible English is :)",
